  status: verified
  fact_type: energy_identity
  review_level: verified
  claim_policy: stable_claim
  claim_summary: "The standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML restores perfect matching and has a reduced normal-incidence dissipative energy identity."
  verification: verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m
  ---
  
  ## statement
  
  For Maxwell-Debye with A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s), the standard stretched-coordinate PML keeps A(s) and replaces partial_i by S_i(s)^{-1} partial_i, S_i=1+sigma_i/s.  At a planar x-interface with S_x=(s+rho)/s, S_y=1, the transmitted normal number is kappa_sc=S_x kappa_0 and the admittance is Y_sc=-kappa_sc/(mu s S_x)=-kappa_0/(mu s), hence the reflection coefficient is zero for every outgoing physical mode.  In the one-dimensional x-PML normal-incidence block, the exact stretched system (partial_t+rho)(epsilon0 epsilon_infty E+P)=partial_x H_y, mu(partial_t+rho)H_y=partial_xE, P+tau P_t=chi E has the positive energy integral 1/2 int (epsilon0 epsilon_infty E^2+mu H_y^2+(1+rho tau)chi^{-1}P^2) dx and derivative -int (rho epsilon0 epsilon_infty E^2+mu rho H_y^2+rho chi^{-1}P^2+tau chi^{-1}P_t^2) dx, up to the usual boundary flux.  Full derivation and full 2D classification: artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md.
  
  ## notes
  
  Generated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.
  
  ### memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-stretched-coordinate-debye-pml-matching-and-energy-gap.md
  ---
  fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:stretched-coordinate-debye-pml-matching-and-energy-gap
  problem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_project: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_task: task-stage3-repaired-model-energy
  predecessors:
    - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched
    - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy
  status: verified
  fact_type: energy_obstruction
  review_level: verified
  claim_policy: stable_claim
  claim_summary: "The standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML is perfectly matched but the naive physical Debye energy has sign-indefinite ADE memory couplings."
  verification: verify-20260620T065326237995Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m
  ---
  
  ## statement
  
  For the repaired Maxwell-Debye PML with Laplace stretch factors S_i(s) applied to spatial derivatives and with the physical Debye law left as (1+tau s)P=chi E, a planar x-interface with S_y=1 has transmitted normal symbol nu=S_x nu0 and admittance Y_+=S_x^{-1}nu/(mu s)=nu0/(mu s)=Y0, so the continuous interface is perfectly matched. In a time-domain ADE realization of the classical stretch S_i=1+sigma_i/s, the positive physical Debye energy E_phys=1/2 int(eps0 eps_inf E^2+mu H_x^2+mu H_y^2+chi^{-1}P^2) has derivative -int tau/chi P_t^2 plus the sign-indefinite memory couplings int[E(psi_E,x-psi_E,y)-H_x psi_Hx,y+H_y psi_Hy,x]. Therefore the v2 monotone energy identity does not transfer to the exact stretched-coordinate PML without a new augmented/passive-memory energy. See artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md.
  
  ## notes
  
  Generated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.
  
  ### memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-baffet-primitive-stretched-debye-2d-energy.md
  ---
  fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:baffet-primitive-stretched-debye-2d-energy
  problem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
