  ### memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md
  ---
  fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched
  problem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_project: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_task: task-stage3-perfect-matching-test
  predecessors:
    - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy
  status: verified
  fact_type: obstruction
  review_level: verified
  claim_policy: stable_claim
  claim_summary: "The v2 covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched."
  verification: verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d
  ---
  
  ## statement
  
  For a planar x-interface with constant layer coefficient rho_x=rho>0, rho_y=0, Laplace parameter Re s>0, and tangential Fourier number k_y, the physical Maxwell-Debye admittance is Y0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2), where A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s).  The v2 covariantly damped model has Yrho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)), where A_rho(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau(s+rho)).  Hence Yrho^2-Y0^2=-rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], which is generically nonzero.  Therefore the interface reflection coefficient (Y0-Yrho)/(Y0+Yrho) is generically nonzero: the model is dissipative but not perfectly matched.  Full derivation: artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md.
  
  ## notes
  
  Generated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.
  
  ### memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md
  ---
  fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction
  problem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_project: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
