     140	
     141	Define
     142	\[
     143	\alpha=1+2a\tau,\qquad
     144	\beta=a+b\tau,\qquad
     145	\gamma=a^2+b(1+a\tau).
     146	\]
     147	The Baffet-Debye energy is
     148	\[
     149	\boxed{
     150	\begin{aligned}
     172	Test (1) with \(u_t+a u\).  The nondispersive part gives the usual Baffet
     173	calculation:
